<title>USA: Core Industries names financial officer.</title>
<headline>Core Industries names financial officer.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMFIELD HILLS, Mich. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Core Industries Inc said Monday that Mark MacGuidwin joined the company as vice president of finance and chief financial officer, effective immediately.</p>
<p>He succeeds Raymond Steben, who left the company earlier in the year.  </p>
<p>MacGuidwin had been vice president-controller of Varity Corp, which previously merged with Lucas Industries Plc to form LucasVarity Plc.</p>
<p>Core Industries makes specialty products in the fluid control and construction products; test, measurement and control, and specialty farm equipment segments.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
